#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
sensortop - a btop-style temperature monitor built on lm-sensors.

Reads the output of `sensors -j` (falling back to plain text), draws
gradient bars in the terminal, a braille history chart and min/max/avg
statistics for the selected sensor.

Settings, chip aliases and the list of manually hidden sensors live in
~/.config/sensortop/config.toml (the `W` key saves the current state).

Usage:
    ./sensortop                # TUI, refresh every 2 s
    ./sensortop -i 1           # refresh every 1 s
    ./sensortop -1             # one-off text dump (no TUI)
    ./sensortop -1 --json      # normalised JSON on stdout (alerting)
    ./sensortop --demo         # synthetic data (no lm-sensors)
    ./sensortop -f             # degrees Fahrenheit
"""

